    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_244b522604d003304ddcd387e7020d5c6d89e5c795360bd482c5c192562c9b95",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Jacobi inversion, completion, and recentering package zeta into an even entire function whose real-rootedness is equivalent to RH, but symmetry and reality on the real axis do not produce zeros there. A later Fourier-moment route illustrates an additional mechanism: eventual sign would control high moments and derivative signs, which are then compared with kernel-derivative decay at the analytic-strip boundary.",
