      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_55b9b142cc288ba1d05ea6d872019ea179bd23d6a292d9f0fe3756871bfed8c5",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Phase rotation makes critical-line zeros accessible through real sign changes, but Gram intervals are sampling cells rather than reliable one-zero containers. A bounded RH certificate is obtained only by composing the resulting lower bound on distinct on-line witnesses with an independently controlled total zero count for the same region.",
